# React rules

## General

Don't import React, e.g. `import React from 'react'`. Instead use statements like `import { useState } from 'react'`.

## Build system

I'm using yarn. You should use yarn instead of npm.

Running the build takes a long time, so you should be reluctant to run this unless necessary.
In general, you should pause and ask me to run a build, then i will show you the error, or you can access the build output in ./.next

## Components

Use const/ES6 arrow functions for component defintions by default.

## Props

Always use the `PageProps` type in ./lib/types.ts for components which are pages. Do not modify this type, use a generic with specifics parameters for expected parameters and search params if these are expected.
Use `type` statements for props.
Comply with ESLint prefer-destructuring rule

## Styling

Use Tailwind CSS for styling whenever possible. Fallback to inline styles only when necessary.

Never use independent css files.
